    "agent_last_message": "Implemented the complete C++20 CLI in `output/` with no external dependencies. The project builds with `cmake -B build && cmake --build build` from [output/CMakeLists.txt](/workspace/output/CMakeLists.txt) and [output/main.cpp](/workspace/output/main.cpp).\n\nThe tool supports `--input` and `--output`, returns exit code `0` on success, `1` for invalid invocation or file I/O failures, and `2` for unexpected internal errors such as `std::bad_alloc`. It follows the spec\u2019s counting rules exactly: byte-counted characters, newline-based line counting, whitespace-delimited words, case-insensitive frequency counting, and top-word ordering by descending count then ascending lexicographic order.\n\nI built it successfully and verified behavior against the spec with these cases: empty file, no trailing newline, trailing newline, multiple consecutive newlines, whitespace-only input, mixed-case words, punctuation retention, and invalid input path handling.",
